# Long-running jobs — visible console

## When this applies

Training, WSL GPU overfit runs, multi-minute decode/diagnostic scripts, and any job where a human may need to spot OOM, divergence, stalls, or stderr warnings in real time.

## Do

- Stream output to a **visible Cursor terminal** (foreground or background shell — user can open the terminal panel).
- **File logging is fine** — use it alongside the console, not instead of it.
- Good patterns:
  - Plain run (console only): `venv\Scripts\python.exe scripts/train_onset_ar.py --config ...`
  - Console **and** file: PowerShell `Tee-Object -FilePath logs/run.log` (duplex), or equivalent tee on other shells.
- After the run, keep log files under `logs/` for later grep / EXP notes when useful.

## Do not

- Use **log-only** redirection as the sole sink (`*> logs/...`, `2>&1 | Out-File`, redirect with no live terminal stream).
- Treat `exit_code: 1` from PowerShell stderr (WSL warnings) as failure without reading the terminal or log — verify whether the job actually completed.

## Summary

| Pattern                  | OK?                                                 |
| ------------------------ | --------------------------------------------------- |
| Console only             | Yes                                                 |
| Console + log file (tee) | Yes — preferred when a durable log helps            |
| Log file only            | No — unless user explicitly asked for log-only mode |
